                            log - open a log file

  Syntax:    log=name,new

  Response:  log/name


Settable parameters:
  name  name of log file (without extension) to be opened in '/usr2/log/'
        The extension '.log' is automatically added. The maximum length of
        'name' is currently 18 characters.

  new   literal 'new' to create the named log if it doesn't already exist, but
        reject the command if it does. Default (null) is to use the named log
        if it already exists or create it if it doesn't. Not displayed in
        monitor responses.

Monitor-only parameters: none

Comments:

When the Field System is initialized, log file 'station' (with extension
'.log') is opened, or created, in directory '/usr2/log'.

The 'new' parameter can be used to require that the named log not already
exist. If it does, the command is rejected with an error. This can be useful,
for example, if you want to make sure you use a new log to record a test.

If the log file requested by this command cannot be opened or created the
Field System returns to using the log file previously in use. If no log file
can be successfully opened, execution of commands or a schedule continues, but
an error message is displayed on the screen at every time to write to the log.
